  "description": "Replace 3 single glazed wooden sash windows with double glazed units. \n\nThe property has 2 sash windows at the front road side of the property and one sash window at the back. All 3 have suffered long term rot damage and need to be replaced. The property is a locally listed building and therefore the replacements will conform to the same design and style and will be of wood construction. \n\nDetails from the contractor 'The London Sash Window Company':\n\nSash Window\n• Removal and legal disposal of old window\n• New made to measure box frame and sashes\n• Grade-A Redwood frame and sashes with hardwood sill*\n• All details (profiles and glazing bars) as per originals\n• Double glazing:\no U-Value = 1.1w/m2K\no White spacer bar\no Argon filled cavity with soft coat low E glass\no Clearer and less reflective glass than traditional double glazing\n• Toughened safety glass fitted where appropriate (BS12150)\n• Traditional weights and pulley wheels where possible, otherwise new springs\n• Draught proof parting and staff beading\n• Long life pre stretched sash cord\n• Trickle vent fitted into top of frame\n• New 3” OGEE architrave and nosing\n• Insurance backed guarantee\nDecoration\n• Sashes treated with preservatives\n• Primer and undercoat applied\n• Painted in White ‘Eggshell’ micro porous paint. RAL9016 Traffic White **\n• All other woodwork (architrave, nosing and sill) fitted and decorated\nWindow Furniture\n• Fitted in polished brass ***\n• New Brighton Fastener\n• Two sash lifts\n• Two exterior ‘D’ handles – white\n• Dual position security bolts and key",
